Use case: identity-preserve.
Asset type: STATIC six-pose mouth-study candidate for the original illustrated wuxia series Ou de Jianghu. This is only a visual mouth-shape study, NOT exact phoneme mapping, NOT a timed animation and NOT validated lip-sync.
Input image 1 is the sole identity, headwear, hair, color and rendering master. Repeat the SAME ONE adult character six times as a contact sheet; do not invent six different people.
Composition: ONE landscape 3:2 sheet, exactly THREE COLUMNS by TWO ROWS, six equal-size head-and-upper-neck portraits. Plain neutral light-grey background, even gutters without drawn borders. Every portrait is straight FRONT VIEW, same eye level, skull scale, same neutral resting eyes and eyebrows, same head angle and gentle studio light. Include each WHOLE head and its original crown/hat/hair ornament inside its panel with a little margin; upper neck and only a sliver of collar, no torso or hands.
Change ONLY the lower lip, upper lip and small credible jaw opening. Reading order left-to-right on top row, then left-to-right bottom row MUST be:
1. fully CLOSED relaxed lips;
2. LIGHTLY PARTED lips, tiny natural opening;
3. A-like moderate vertical oval mouth, restrained jaw opening, not a yawn;
4. E/I-like gently horizontally spread mouth, a narrow natural upper-tooth strip may show, NOT a happy smile or a grin;
5. O-like rounded medium opening;
6. U-like small pursed rounded opening, noticeably smaller than position 5.
Keep six shapes visually distinct without exaggerated black mouth holes. Natural coherent lips, oral cavity, teeth and tongue where actually visible; no double tooth rows, floating teeth, fangs, protruding tongue or warped jaw. Mouth corners remain believable and the face identity does not change. Same restrained expression throughout; no eyebrow, gaze, age or emotion change.
Preserve the master's detailed drawn ornate historical Chinese wuxia style, delicate linework and controlled painted shading. Do not turn photographic, plastic 3D or wooden puppet.
NO letters, numbers, labels, phonetic symbols, speech bubbles, dialogue, text, logos, watermarks, arrows, sound or scenery. Six static head studies only.
Character invariants: Adult slender male Shen Guihe: long straight black hair, narrow grey eyes, pale calm face, tall white/silver crown with its SINGLE white feather. Preserve exact face and hair; no fan or hands enter this head study.

